{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>YHWH's anger shall smoke.</b> Through bodily anger one grows hot and smoke issues from the nose; and so (II Samuel 22:9) ״עָלָה עָשָׁן בְּאַפּוֹ״ — and even though this does not apply to the Omnipresent, Scripture makes the ear hear as it is accustomed and able to hear, according to the way of the world." "<b>And His jealousy.</b> A term of fury — אנפרטמי\"נט בְּלַעַ\"ז — a gripping hold of vengeance, and He does not forgo the measure."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French enfortement / empertement, 'vehement anger'; the phrase אֲחִיזַת לְבִישַׁת נְקָמָה is translated hyper-literally; some witnesses read לְבִישַׁת differently."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:53.074267637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}